# Tests that call mock.module(), mutate process.env, or contain latency-sensitive
# remote-DB fixtures run in their own process. Bun cannot restore module mocks,
# env mutations can overlap, and concurrent integration files saturate the
# disposable Neon compute. These files use the non-discoverable `.isolated.ts`
# suffix; the strict isolated runner executes every entry serially.
# This keeps both bare `bun test` and the shared `bun run test` batch clean.
#
# Keep this in sync: rename any new contaminating or DB-heavy test to
# `.isolated.ts` and add it here before it can affect sibling imports.
# Audit module mocks with: grep -rlE 'mock\.module' src tests --include='*.spec.ts' --include='*.test.ts' --include='*.isolated.ts'
# Audit env writes with: rg 'process\.env\.[A-Z0-9_]+\s*(\?\?=|\|\|=|=)|delete process\.env' src tests
